<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>two-readers-brief.md</title><style>body{font:18px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1rem;color:#17252d;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #777;padding:.5rem}a{color:#064b8c}</style><main><h1>Write a CFO email and an operations update — learner brief</h1>
<p>Fictional Northstar Services training material.</p>
<h2>Approved fictional facts</h2>
<p>F1 September budget USD 200,000.
F2 actual USD 218,000; supplied variance USD 18,000 / 9%.
F3 approved explanation USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel.
F4 forecast revision proposed, unapproved.
F5 operations lead must confirm remaining contractor end date by September 25.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>Northstar&#39;s September cost review is complete. The same approved facts need two internal drafts.</p>
<h2>Actions</h2>
<ol>
<li>Write the reader and requested action for each version.</li>
<li>Give F1–F5 to AI and request both drafts with different emphasis.</li>
<li>Check every number, date, and approval-status verb against the facts.</li>
<li>Revise the CFO version to foreground impact and decision status, and the operations version to foreground the date confirmation.</li>
<li>Record two edits that improved usefulness without changing meaning.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Output</h2>
<p>Audience briefs; CFO email up to 180 words; operations update up to 90 words; fact ledger; revision note.</p>
